 you can use the hook.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Bread? Sounds complicated.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It's not bad. You pop in the bread dough, then push the lid down. You turn the dial around to knead, then press start. When it's done you just scrape it out.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hmmm ...", "id": 2, "time": "16000", "image": "engenn7le18ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm going to borrow a small processor from work this weekend. I'll show you how it works. I'm buying the same type when I can.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: If you wanted me to come over early I could.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: If you did, you would have some extra time to try out the gadgets! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm bringing my camera. I'm going to snap some pictures. Then I'll make a slideshow!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Now that sounds interesting!", "id": 3, "time": "42400", "image": "engenn7le18ob07re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Rice Cookout"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Kitchen Gadgets"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional vs. The Second Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the the present of future.</p><p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "First conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Present verb, + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span> <br/>(you can come over)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Second conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Past verb,    + <span class=\"italic\">would</span> <br/>If you had time, I would help you with that.<br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional<br/>(Cause and Effect)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional<br/>(Hypothetical Situations)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If I want to julienne vegetables, I can purchase a mandoline.</p><p>If you want to slice up vegetables, you use this disc.</p><p>If you make bread, you can use the hook.</p><p>If you come over early, I'll show you how to use it.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>I'd get an expensive food processor if I had the money.</p><p>What could you do with that if you got one?</p><p>If you wanted me to come over early I could.</p><p>If you did, you would have some extra time to try out the gadgets!</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the <span class=\"italic\">IF</span> clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (<span class=\"italic\">I would</span> = <span class=\"italic\">I'd</span>)"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future with <span class=\"italic\">Will</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Going to</span>, the Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use three different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about  things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Deciding Now</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll show you how it works.<br/>Then I'll make a slideshow!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Intentions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going to look at all the other kitchen gadgets!<br/>I'm going to borrow a small processor from work this weekend.<br/>I'm going to snap some pictures.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">A Plan / Things On the Agenda</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm getting more as soon as I have the money!<br/>I'm buying the same type when I can.<br/>I'm bringing my camera.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to turn around"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move from one side to the other"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Turn the dial all the way around."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in the kitchen appliance department."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to scrape out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use a spatula to remove food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use the spatula to scrape the rice out of the pot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to push down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to apply pressure to"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Please push the lid down."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pop in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put something inside another thing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You pop in the bread dough, then bake it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to slice up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cut with a sharp knife"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use this disc to slice up the vegetables with the food processor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to julienne"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cut into long thin strips"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to julienne some vegetables for the salad."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "food processor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a kitchen appliance for chopping, mixing, or pureeing foods"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd get an expensive food processor if I had the money."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mandoline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hand gadget used to slice food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can purchase a mandoline to slice the vegetables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le18ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of  a kitchen gadget you use often (e.g. garlic press, blender, toaster oven, rice cooker)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write an explanation about how to use the gadget in about 100 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use some phrasal verbs in your explanation (e.g. Blender: <span class=\"italic\">you push the lid down</span>, etc.)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of what other types food and dishes you could use the gadget for  (e.g. <span class=\"italic\">If you want, you could use a toaster to warm up leftovers</span>)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your explanation to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I explain how to use a kitchen gadget. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about cooking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my explanation with a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}